CommitmentForm still targets the wrong dashboard instance – the form is instantiated with parent_dashboard=self.parent_dashboard inside CommitmentTrackerWidget.add_commitment() instead of self, so the dialog never reaches DashboardMain for cache updates or logging (@ui/dashboard_main.py#2258-2284). Inside the form, all refreshes and 
_emit_commitment_delta()
 calls therefore operate on the widget rather than the main window (@ui/commitment_form.py#518-727).
Signal wiring stops at the widget – CommitmentTrackerWidget defines handle_commitment_added_signal() but nothing connects a signal directly to DashboardMain. The dialog emits commitment_added and connects to the widget, yet the widget merely forwards to self.parent_dashboard.handle_commitment_delta, which doesn’t exist, so the slot is never resolved (@ui/dashboard_main.py#2258-2284).
DashboardMain has no commitment cache or delta handler – no attributes track current_unpaid_commitments_total, no handle_commitment_delta, and no logging hooks for commitment deltas anywhere in DashboardMain. All balance recomputation still pulls from the database each refresh without any cached baseline or signal-driven adjustments (@ui/dashboard_main.py#330-610, @ui/dashboard_main.py#3535-3545).
Other files don’t provide the missing slot/caching logic – searches across core/ and ui/ show helpers like balance_helper.get_unpaid_commitments_total() and 
commitment_form._emit_commitment_delta()
, but no class caches current_unpaid_commitments_total or exposes a handle_commitment_delta-style slot. No alternative dashboard class implements this either.
Conclusion: the repo currently lacks the necessary Dashboard-level fields and slot implementation to support event-driven balance adjustments. To finish the wiring, we’ll need to (1) pass self into 
CommitmentForm
, (2) connect the dialog signal straight to DashboardMain, (3) add cached commitment totals plus a handle_commitment_delta method (with logging) on DashboardMain, and (4) update widgets to use that cache. Let me know when you’re ready for that change set.

