when a commitment is made what is the flow from plaid display to subtracting values? tell me the files, classes and methods used 

Here’s the end‑to‑end path when you add a commitment and see “Available Balance” / “Price After Commitments” update:

Dashboard metrics pull Plaid + commitments
DashboardMain.setup_metrics_carousel(...)
 builds the balance cards and calls 
load_real_data()
 to gather inputs (@ui/dashboard_main.py#300-420).
load_real_data()
:
Queries the user’s checking account(s) and, if a Plaid token exists, calls core.plaid_api.get_account_balances to fetch the live “available” balance (@ui/dashboard_main.py#497-564).
Falls back to a transaction sum if Plaid isn’t available (@ui/dashboard_main.py#526-541).
Calculates unpaid commitments with a SQL sum on category_commitments (@ui/dashboard_main.py#583-593).
Derives available_balance = checking_balance and price_after_commitments = checking_balance - commitments and renders the cards (@ui/dashboard_main.py#595-420).
Committing a new recurring expense
The “Add Commitment” form lives in 
CommitmentForm
 (class in 
ui/commitment_form.py
). When you press save:
save_commitment_background()
 inserts the new row into category_commitments (ensuring extra columns exist) (@ui/commitment_form.py#587-623).
After insert, the form calls the parent dashboard’s 
commitment_tracker.load_commitments()
 plus 
refresh_metrics_cards_main()
 and 
refresh_dashboard()
 so the Plaid/commitment cards rebuild with the new total (@ui/commitment_form.py#624-659).
A follow‑up timer forces another metrics refresh to guarantee “Price After Commitments” reflects the new subtraction (@ui/commitment_form.py#644-664).
Support helpers
If other modules need the same numbers, 
core.balance_helper.get_checking_balance
 and 
get_unpaid_commitments_total
 encapsulate the identical Plaid → fallback and commitment sum logic (@core/balance_helper.py#11-81).
So the flow is: Plaid balance is loaded in 
DashboardMain.load_real_data()
 → commitments sum is pulled in the same method → cards display both values. When you create a commitment via 
CommitmentForm
, it writes to category_commitments, then triggers the dashboard’s refresh hooks so the next 
load_real_data()
 call subtracts the new amount from “Price After Commitments.”

