hat about balance helper.py?

core/balance_helper.py
 is the shared utility module that backs the dashboard math when Plaid isn’t enough on its own:

get_checking_balance(user_id)
Prioritizes data sources in this order:
accounts.simulated_balance (developer override).
Live Plaid balance via core.plaid_api.get_account_balances.
Fallback to summing transactions (income minus expense) from the transactions table.
That way, any caller outside 
DashboardMain
 can still ask for “what should the checking card show?” and get the same number the UI uses. (@core/balance_helper.py#11-64)
get_unpaid_commitments_total(user_id)
Runs a single SELECT COALESCE(SUM(amount),0) against category_commitments filtered to is_paid=0, returning the total outstanding commitments. This mirrors the computation inside 
DashboardMain.load_real_data()
 and is used whenever another feature (e.g., analytics) needs the same “Price After Commitments” subtraction. (@core/balance_helper.py#67-80)
In short, 
balance_helper.py
 centralizes the Plaid/simulated/transaction logic so other modules don’t have to reimplement the priority order or SQL.

