For a true instant update, the event-driven approach (Option 2) is the fastest and most precise:

When the user hits “Save” or “Mark as Paid,” emit a Qt signal with the delta (added commitment amount or paid commitment amount).
DashboardMain
 listens to that signal and updates a cached unpaid_commitments_total (subtract/add) before calling a lightweight render_price_after_cards() method—no full dashboard rebuild required.
Behind the scenes, periodic or on-navigation refreshes still run the full SQL to keep things honest.
This gives you the immediate “quick refresh” effect you’re looking for, avoids the latency of re-running 
load_real_data()
 every time, and is relatively low-risk to implement compared to revamping the schema or introducing a brand-new state service.

